= Overview =

PKI provides tools to upgrade the internal LDAP database. See [https://www.dogtagpki.org/wiki/Database_Upgrade Database Upgrade].

= Displaying Database Status (Not Implemented Yet) =

<pre>
$ pki-server db-status
  Hostname: server.example.com
  Port: 636
  SSL: yes
  Client Certificate: subsystemCert pki-tomcat
</pre>

= Database Upgrade =

The pki-server db-upgrade is a tool to upgrade PKI server LDAP database. Currently the upgrade includes:
* [https://fedorahosted.org/pki/ticket/1667 Ticket #1667: adding issuerName attribute]

See the [https://git.fedorahosted.org/cgit/pki.git/tree/base/server/python/pki/server/cli/db.py source code] for details.

This tool is used as part of [https://www.dogtagpki.org/wiki/Database_Upgrade_for_PKI_10.2.x Database Upgrade for PKI 10.2.x]. To run the database upgrade:

<pre>
$ pki-server db-upgrade
----------------
Upgrade complete
----------------
</pre>

= Schema Upgrade =

The pki-server db-schema-upgrade is a tool to upgrade PKI server LDAP schema. Currently the upgrade includes:
* re-applying [https://git.fedorahosted.org/cgit/pki.git/tree/base/server/share/conf/schema.ldif /usr/share/pki/server/conf/schema.ldif]

See the [https://git.fedorahosted.org/cgit/pki.git/tree/base/server/python/pki/server/cli/db.py source code] for details.

<pre>
$ pki-server db-schema-upgrade -D "cn=Directory Manager" -w Secret.123
----------------
Upgrade complete
----------------
</pre>

See also the following tickets:
* [https://fedorahosted.org/pki/ticket/2319 Ticket #2319: Add / revise vlv indexes for KRA due to realm changes]
* [https://fedorahosted.org/pki/ticket/2320 Ticket #2320: Add db migration scripts for schema, vlv and index changes]

